# kde/manifest - the single source for every Qt 6 and KDE template in this repo
#
# tools/kde-gen writes <cat>/<pkg>/template from this file. tools/kde-bump
# rewrites the version lines, the checksums and the license lines. Edit here,
# never in a generated template.
#
# Sets. One version per set; kde-bump finds the newest stable release of each.
#
#   set NAME VERSION
#
# Packages. One block each, ended by "end":
#
#   pkg NAME             bpm package name
#     set SET            frameworks, plasma, gear, qt or standalone
#     cat DIR            category folder the template goes in
#     src NAME           tarball base name when it differs from the package name
#     version V          standalone packages only
#     url URL            standalone packages only; ${version} stays literal
#     watch TYPE ARGS    standalone only, how kde-bump finds new versions:
#                          kde-flat INDEX [NAME]  files NAME-VER.tar.xz in INDEX
#                          kde-dirs INDEX         directories VER/ in INDEX
#                          github OWNER/REPO      newest vX.Y.Z tag
#     home URL           home_page
#     desc TEXT          short_desc
#     license LIST       SPDX names, comma separated (kde-bump reads LICENSES/)
#     depends LIST       runtime and link dependencies (also put in make_depends)
#     make LIST          build-only dependencies
#     run LIST           runtime-only dependencies (not put in make_depends)
#     args ARGS          extra cmake arguments
#     x11 OPTION         cmake option switched by the x11 use flag (!OPTION = inverted)
#     docs MODE          no, optional (kdoctools when man or doc is on) or required
#     network yes        allow_network=yes (Rust crates fetched at build time)
#     revision N         template revision, reset to 1 by a version bump
#     checksum B3        blake3 of the tarball, written by kde-bump
#   end
#
# Dependencies were seeded from Alpine's APKBUILDs (musl, known to build),
# mapped to Basix names, then checked against every CMakeLists.txt of the
# tagged sources for REQUIRED entries. Patches live in kde/patches/<pkg>/.

